{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_1>\n__author__ = 'MoonBall'\n\nimport sys\n# sys.stdin = open('data/D.in', 'r')\nT = 1\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef solve():\n    P, K = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    if K == 0:\n        print(pow(P, P - 1, MOD))\n        return\n    \n    # Build the mapping: f(x) = (K * x) % P\n    mapping = [(K * x) % P for x in range(P)]\n    \n    # Track visited nodes and count cycle lengths\n    visited = [False] * P\n    cycle_counts = [0] * P\n    \n    for start in range(P):\n        if visited[start]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Traverse the cycle starting from 'start'\n        length = 0\n        current = start\n        while not visited[current]:\n            visited[current] = True\n            current = mapping[current]\n            length += 1\n        \n        cycle_counts[length] += 1\n    \n    # Compute the answer\n    result = 1\n    for cycle_len in range(1, P):\n        if cycle_counts[cycle_len] == 0:\n            continue\n        \n        # For each cycle of length 'cycle_len', we have:\n        # effective_count = cycle_len * cycle_counts[cycle_len] + (cycle_counts[1] if cycle_len > 1 else 0)\n        effective_count = cycle_len * cycle_counts[cycle_len] + (cycle_counts[1] if cycle_len > 1 else 0)\n        result = (result * pow(effective_count, cycle_counts[cycle_len], MOD)) % MOD\n    \n    print(result)\n\nfor _ in range(T):\n    solve()\n</your_rewritten_code_1>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int T = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < T; i++) {\n            solve(sc);\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void solve(Scanner sc) {\n        int P = sc.nextInt();\n        int K = sc.nextInt();\n\n        if (K == 0) {\n            System.out.println(modPow(P, P - 1, MOD));\n            return;\n        }\n\n        // Build the mapping: f(x) = (K * x) % P\n        int[] mapping = new int[P];\n        for (int x = 0; x < P; x++) {\n            mapping[x] = (int) ((long) K * x % P);\n        }\n\n        // Track visited nodes and count cycle lengths\n        boolean[] visited = new boolean[P];\n        int[] cycleCounts = new int[P];\n\n        for (int start = 0; start < P; start++) {\n            if (visited[start]) {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            // Traverse the cycle starting from 'start'\n            int length = 0;\n            int current = start;\n            while (!visited[current]) {\n                visited[current] = true;\n                current = mapping[current];\n                length++;\n            }\n\n            cycleCounts[length]++;\n        }\n\n        // Compute the answer\n        long result = 1;\n        for (int cycleLen = 1; cycleLen < P; cycleLen++) {\n            if (cycleCounts[cycleLen] == 0) {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            // For each cycle of length 'cycleLen', we have:\n            // effective_count = cycleLen * cycleCounts[cycleLen] + (cycleCounts[1] if cycleLen > 1 else 0)\n            long effectiveCount = (long) cycleLen * cycleCounts[cycleLen] + (cycleLen > 1 ? cycleCounts[1] : 0);\n            result = (result * modPow(effectiveCount, cycleCounts[cycleLen], MOD)) % MOD;\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(result);\n    }\n\n    static long modPow(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        base %= mod;\n        long result = 1;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * base) % mod;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00011014331539627165, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00040046300273388624, -3.2066785934148356e-05, -0.11288411170244217, -0.2591368854045868, -1.156323378381785e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -8.427741704508662e-05, -0.043000709265470505, -0.0019289711490273476, -0.1966472864151001, -0.00010024998482549563, -0.012555954977869987, -2.9802276912960224e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -4.172316494077677e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.6587049961090088, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.004630556795746088, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.003600901225581765, -0.008615585044026375, -1.311301275563892e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -4.5536911784438416e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.156323378381785e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -6.12716976320371e-05, -0.12738794088363647, -7.152531907195225e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.152531907195225e-06, -4.410734163684538e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.00044347942457534373, -0.011629643850028515, -6.437280717364047e-06, -1.1920928244535389e